From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: dt_idle_genpd: don't fail on a parent domain that probes later

dt_idle_pd_init_topology() links every PM domain in the PSCI node to the
domain its power-domains names, and gives up on all of them if one link
fails. A parent outside the CPU idle domains, such as the Qualcomm MPM
wakeup interrupt controller, is a platform device that probes at
device_initcall time or later, while the PSCI domains are set up before
that and psci-cpuidle, a faux device created at device_initcall time,
can't wait. On msm8953 with the MPM as parent of the system domain the
domains returned -EPROBE_DEFER and the CPUs were left without cpuidle.

Skip a link whose parent isn't there yet, so the CPU idle domains come
up, and leave that link to the parent's driver.

---
 drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_genpd.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_genpd.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_genpd.c
@@ -142,6 +142,15 @@
 		child.args_count = 0;
 		ret = of_genpd_add_subdomain(&parent, &child);
 		of_node_put(parent.np);
+		/*
+		 * A parent outside the CPU idle domains, such as a wakeup
+		 * interrupt controller, may probe later than CPU idle can
+		 * wait for. Leave the link to its driver.
+		 */
+		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
+			pr_info("%pOF: parent domain not ready, not linked\n", node);
+			continue;
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
